# Drafted by Gemini (R11 batch b4), edited. mrs_oakum's first conversation.

~ start
set mrs_oakum_met
Narrator: Cold tallow and wet dog hang about her apron as she pares grey fat from a knucklebone.
mrs_oakum [weary]: Talk to the master up front for prime cuts. I only scrape troughs and haul the bone-bucket out back.
-> menu

~ menu
mrs_oakum [neutral]: Speak quick if you need something. The clock don't wait on idle tongues.
* Ask what keeps her working out back -> work
* Ask what she makes of Wickermoor Village -> village
* Ask if she has heard any strange talk -> rumour
* [Medicine DC 14] Note the raw chain-scars around her wrists -> secret_ok | secret_fail
* Take our leave -> END

~ work
mrs_oakum [weary]: Folks leave me be, and I get the gristle and marrow-ends to carry home before the Evening bell.
mrs_oakum [afraid]: Once that bell tolls, I lock myself out on the high scrub till Twilight comes round.
-> menu

~ village
mrs_oakum [neutral]: Folk pray to their thirsty tree and trust the hedges. A fence only keeps in what wants to stay.
-> menu

~ rumour
mrs_oakum [sad]: Foul water seeps from Skitterdeep mine, north-west in the crags. The creek tastes of copper and bad fever, and the beasts know it.
-> menu

~ secret_ok
Narrator: Coarse grey hairs bristle on her scarred forearms, and her breath catches at raw liver on the block.
mrs_oakum [afraid]: Eyes to yourself, stranger. Only a heavy chain and butcher's offal keep my teeth out of this town come dark.
-> menu

~ secret_fail
mrs_oakum [angry]: Best not stare at a working woman's hands while she holds a cleaver, friend. Mind your own business.
-> menu
